vineyards dominate the landscape around  Carcassonne in southern France the  Languedoc Roussillon region is the  largest wine growing area in the country  different varieties of grape are able to  flourish in the soil here at domaine du  lac near caucus on you can sample top  quality wines and food  the former vineyard estate is now a  luxury hotel and has been a family  business for generations wine is the  perfect ingredient for star chef  Philippe Dacians recipes this is a dry  Blanc de lis more sparkling wine from  the region I use it as the base for the  sauce in my porcini ravioli dish the  pearls in a sparkling wine gives a dish  creamy consistency which works very well  with the light nutty note contributed by  the porcini mushrooms  Budhan was that salmon on top of a  porcini ravioli in a sparkling wine  sauce is a light starter and today euro  Max has the recipe  first dice the onions and lightly saute  them in olive oil with a little butter  then chop up the porcini x' these are  porcini mushrooms that grew under  chestnut trees and these grew under  Pines because the pine needles often  fall on the mushrooms and they get less  sunlight they're lighter in color you  know chestnuts stand on the other hand  the sun's rays penetrate the foliage so  the mushrooms have a darker color  the mushrooms provide the base for both  the filling and the sauce glaze the  mushrooms and onions with sparkling wine  we reduced the whole thing until the  liquids gone because the mushroom should  completely absorb the wine for the  filling add cream and for the sauce add  stock cream and a bit of butter puree  the mixture and flavor with salt and  pepper  now we had a few drops of nut oil that  brings out the mushroom flavor and the  earthy woody aroma  that's the sauce shouldn't be heated  above 60 degrees Celsius or it'll lose  its nutty taste place the filling on the  pasta dough brush the edges with egg  yolk and carefully seal it it's very  important to ensure that all the air is  pressed out of the ravioli come on  otherwise they burst during cooking  Cecchetti  now turn off the heat  Sommelier honk Cikini is responsible for  the wine selection at domaine du lac  with more than 600 types of wines stored  in the wine cellar the sommelier can  really base his recommendation on the  Preferences of his guests I recommend  this wine with the ravio it's 80%  climatically with clean ash bla  it has a slight mineral note and was  matured in an oak barrel so it also has  a light smoky woody flavor very elegant  very smooth  garnish the ravioli with the porcini  mushrooms that have been sauteed in  butter and the starter for a wintry menu  he's ready for the table and a glass of  ganache to go with it the perfect way to  get into the right mood as the end of  the year approaches  you
 

